1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,700
Maya just joined the team, and asks the agent to explain the checkout queue as a video.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:15,333
Unblackbox turns that ask into a narrated video. Let's follow it from question to finished file.

3
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:24,933
First, the agent reads the skill: rules for videos people actually understand, taken from learning research.

4
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:31,433
Then it maps the system and writes one JSON spec, a list of beats.

5
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:39,500
A beat pairs one sentence with what appears on screen, so the picture never drifts from the voice.

6
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:47,667
Inside the tool, the spec passes four parts: a checker, a voice, a timeline, and a renderer.

7
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:53,967
Follow queue dot JSON through all four, from file to frames.

8
00:00:54,967 --> 00:01:02,167
The checker blocks broken specs, and warns when a video gets too dense, wordy, or low level.

9
00:01:03,167 --> 00:01:11,833
The voice is Kokoro, a free local speech model. Each sentence is cached, so edits re-voice only changes.

10
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:19,400
The timeline turns seconds into frames. Each beat lasts its sentence, plus a breath.

11
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:27,867
The renderer draws every frame with React, using Remotion, and writes the video with subtitles.

12
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:35,667
A render takes as long as the video plays. What if the agent needs five layout fixes?

13
00:01:40,667 --> 00:01:47,967
It never renders to check. The still command draws every beat into one image in five seconds.

14
00:01:48,967 --> 00:01:54,233
Only when the sheet looks right does it render, once, in the background.

15
00:01:55,233 --> 00:02:03,000
Maya can also play with the queue. A playground app reuses the same board: press events, click parts.

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,200
The player is built once. Each new playground is only data, ready in about twenty seconds.

17
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:18,467
In the repo: the tool lives in source, the rules in the skill, the player in play.

18
00:02:19,467 --> 00:02:26,667
One ask, one spec, one video. New here? Start with the agents guide and the examples.
